{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/838589-1-on-1-st-gm-dm-ing","id":838589,"title":"1 on 1 ST/GM/DM - ing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-28T05:25:33-08:00","id":838589,"title":"1 on 1 ST/GM/DM - ing","content":"Just tried a 1 on 1 session of some Savage Worlds cyberpunk with my fiance and I have to say it's bloody exhausting. I enjoyed doing it, any way to get a game session in, but something about doing it 1 on 1 is really tiring. I'm going to try to get more into the spirit of it and get better at it but I'm not sure it's something I can regularly do.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any experience or advice to offer for this type of game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T08:49:11-08:00","id":838661,"title":"","content":"I looooooooove 1 on 1 games. You can get much more involved in the little things that get glossed over when you have to share the spotlight between multiple PCs. But yeah, it can definitely be more tiring, for both the GM and the player. I like to do it in some kind of text medium. Gives me more time to formulate my narration than real-time, which reduces stress and helps me keep at it without getting too worn out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:06:34-08:00","id":838668,"title":"","content":"Well the fiance and I already do text medium types of RPs but they're mainly novel like with no real 'rules' attributed to them...But maybe I'll try it out anyway, see if it works better that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:48:24-08:00","id":838688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lilappleblossom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/838589-1-on-1-st-gm-dm-ing?p=838668#post838668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the fiance and I already do text medium types of RPs but they're mainly novel like with no real 'rules' attributed to them...But maybe I'll try it out anyway, see if it works better that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I like to integrate game rules into that sort of novel-style roleplay. It takes a little bit of practice to get used to, but you basically just use the dice to add some degree of randomness to your narrative. Instead of describing what the character does and the results together, describe what they do, figure out the best way to resolve that action within the game system (whether that be a simple &quot;it works&quot; or &quot;it doesn't work&quot; or something crunchier like a skill check), and then describe the results based on the roll. That's my approach, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:48:37-08:00","id":838689,"title":"","content":"I can't speak for Savage Worlds but with World of Darkness at least it's pretty easy. Like Charlaquin pointed out generally when STing for a group you have a lot of players pulling their own way, or when you get them to go after a singular goal arguing about how exactly to deal with it. I decided to try one on ones when a group I was in spent 30 minutes standing in a room and deciding which of two doors to open.<br /> <br /> I've found the more combat-intensive the game is, the more work it takes for the DM in a one on one story. Especially when things like area of effect and range are a matter of life or death for the character. One way to help get you into the swing of things might be to take some time before the game starts and run through the game as if you were playing it. Since you're just doing it yourself and not really requiring dice rolls it's just a thought exercise, but it can let you catch things you may have missed. If a scene requires the group to ford a treacherous river, for instance, you might want to have some extra notes on swimming or dangerous waters. You can also use this time to make sure everything is mechanically balanced, as traditional rpg monsters are balanced against a group of 4 players of wide skill sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T18:48:40-08:00","id":838902,"title":"","content":"I've done 1-on-1 games with a variety of different systems, though not Savage Worlds.<br /> <br /> The reason why not Savage Worlds, in fact, is because of the thing I noticed while doing this: The better systems to use for 1-on-1 play are the ones which the GM/ST/DM is proficient enough with to not even hesitate about how to proceed with any rules interaction that might come up. For me, that means AD&amp;D, D&amp;D 5th edition, Shadowrun 3rd edition, Call of Cthulhu, and Vampire: the Masquerade (specifically revised, restricted to core book only) are the current systems that I can run 1-on-1 (though I am aiming at expanding that list).<br /> <br /> As for the stories told in 1-on-1 games, I prefer them to focus closely on the character - which means the player needs to have a character that has goals and ideas of how to achieve those goals. That way, the player is able to lead the story and I am more able to just be reacting, placing what seems a natural fit in front of them for wherever it is they take the character. I find that much easier than having a plan of where things are going and hoping that the player follows the trail - not having other players to fill some time deliberating about course of action to take to buy me the time to adjust a plan at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}